# Every Horde flight path in the Eastern Kingdoms, from Undercity out to the level 60 zones, roughly in
# the order of the zones' levels. Polestar knows which flight paths a character has, so each step a
# character already has is passed over: the tour always picks up at the first flight path still
# missing.
#
# The flight points and their flight masters come from Polestar's reference data. Rog'mar in the
# Riverglades is WoW Forever's own: Polestar's data has it since 0.4.0, and it still names its flight
# master (npc).

guide flight-path-collector/horde-eastern-kingdoms
title Flight Paths: Eastern Kingdoms (Horde)
faction Horde
category Exploration
folder Flight paths
levels 1-60
zone map 1415
keywords flight path, flight paths, flight point, flight points, flight master, wind rider, bat, FP, taxi, Riverglades
why Every flight path you learn is a walk you never make again, and the tour skips the ones you already have.
version 2

step Undercity
  zone Undercity
  tip The Forsaken capital under the ruins of Lordaeron, in Tirisfal Glades. The zeppelins to Orgrimmar and Grom'gol leave from the tower outside the ruins.
  getfp "Undercity"

step The Sepulcher
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip The Forsaken outpost in the middle of Silverpine Forest (levels 10-20), south of Tirisfal Glades.
  getfp "The Sepulcher"

step Tarren Mill
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip The Forsaken town in the north-east of Hillsbrad Foothills (levels 20-30).
  getfp "Tarren Mill"

step Hammerfall
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip The Horde town in the east of the Arathi Highlands (levels 30-40).
  getfp "Hammerfall"

step Grom'gol
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip The Horde base camp in the north of Stranglethorn Vale (levels 30-45), where the zeppelins from Undercity and Orgrimmar land.
  getfp "Grom'gol"

step Booty Bay
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip The goblin port at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale, with a flight master for each faction. The boat from Ratchet lands here too.
  getfp "Booty Bay"

step Stonard
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip The orc fortress in the middle of the Swamp of Sorrows (levels 35-45). The road in from Duskwood crosses Deadwind Pass, whose creatures are well above level 50: keep to it.
  getfp "Stonard"

step Rog'mar
  zone Riverglades
  tip The Horde camp in the middle of the Riverglades, WoW Forever's own zone north of the Swamp of Sorrows (levels 36-44). The step ticks itself when Grakna's flight map opens (with a Polestar older than 0.4, tick it off yourself).
  getfp "Rog'mar" npc 255993

step Kargath
  zone Badlands
  tip The Horde outpost on the western edge of the Badlands (levels 35-45). From the Riverglades a way climbs north into the south of the Badlands.
  getfp "Kargath"

step Thorium Point
  zone Searing Gorge
  tip The Thorium Brotherhood's camp on the north-west rim of the Searing Gorge (levels 43-50). The trail into the Gorge starts in the Badlands, a short way from Kargath.
  getfp "Thorium Point"

step Flame Crest
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip The Horde camp in the north of the Burning Steppes (levels 50-58). From the Searing Gorge the way through Blackrock Mountain comes out in the Steppes.
  getfp "Flame Crest"

step Revantusk Village
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip The Revantusk trolls' village on the east coast of the Hinterlands (levels 40-50). The road in from Hillsbrad Foothills crosses the whole zone.
  getfp "Revantusk Village"

step Light's Hope Chapel
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip The Argent Dawn's chapel at the east end of the Eastern Plaguelands (levels 53-60), the last Horde flight path in the Eastern Kingdoms: for the other continent, open Flight Paths: Kalimdor (Horde).
  getfp "Light's Hope Chapel"
